          "content": "Awesome! Now let me create the implementation plan. Based on the existing codebase and our lore, here's the structured plan:\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan - Spec 3.1: Demo Experience\n\n### Problem Statement\n\nNew players need a compelling, guided introduction to Waypoint that teaches mechanics naturally, establishes the world's tone, and demonstrates the \"AI + real game state\" differentiator through a 20+ turn playable demo.\n\n### Requirements\n\n- Opening narration at The Waystone with Lenna as first contact\n- 5 NPCs (Lenna, Aran, Adrian, Helga, The Wanderer)\n- 3 quests (Welcome tutorial, Boar Hunt, Berry Gathering)\n- Peaceful prairie setting with easy combat tutorial\n- Relationship-gated rewards (Lenna's Token at +2)\n- Random Wanderer encounters (10-20% when traveling)\n- 20-turn demo scenario without errors\n\n### Background\n\nThe codebase already has:\n- Streaming turn system (`/api/turn/stream`)\n- Content safety filtering (`lib/safety/sentinel.ts`)\n- Character creation flow\n- Basic seed data structure (one location seeded)\n- Turn validation and event application\n- Skill check mechanics with roll UI\n\n### Proposed Solution\n\nImplement in 6 phases: seed data → first turn flow → NPCs → quests → combat → polish. Each phase builds on the previous and ends with testable functionality.\n\n---\n\n### Task Breakdown\n\n**Task 1: Create Database Seed Data**\n\nObjective: Populate Supabase with all starter locations, NPCs, quests, and world news.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Create `supabase/migrations/20260104_demo_seed_data.sql` with INSERT statements for:\n  - 3 locations: The Waystone, Nomante Outpost, Windhollow Wilderness\n  - 5 NPCs: Lenna, Aran Nomante, Adrian, Helga, The Wanderer\n  - 3 quests: Welcome to Windhollow, The Boar Hunt, Berry Gathering\n  - 2 world news entries (waystone activation rumor, peaceful prairie)\n- Add corresponding TypeScript constants in `constants.ts` for client-side reference\n- Include enemy template for wild boar (easy tier)\n\nDemo: Run migration, verify data appears in Supabase dashboard.\n\n---\n\n**Task 2: Implement First Turn Initialization**\n\nObjective: When character creation completes, initialize world state and generate opening narration.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Update `POST /api/character` to create initial world state with:\n  - Location: The Waystone\n  - Region: Windhollow Vale\n  - Time: Day 1, Morning\n  - Weather: Clear\n  - Entities: [\"lenna\"] (scholar present at waystone)\n- Create opening narration template in `constants.ts` describing awakening at waystone, Lenna's presence\n- Generate first turn automatically with suggested actions: \"Talk to the scholar\", \"Examine the waystone\", \"Look around\", \"Check yourself\"\n- Player starts with cloth armor only, 0 gold, empty inventory\n\nDemo: Create new character → see opening narration with Lenna present → suggested actions appear.\n\n---\n\n**Task 3: Implement NPC Interaction System**\n\nObjective: Enable \"Talk to [NPC]\" actions with relationship tracking and dialogue generation.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Update `lib/gemini/prompts.ts` to include NPC data in context when NPC is in current location entities\n- Add NPC personality and dialogue hints to prompt for Chronicler\n- Implement relationship change events (`relationship_change` type already exists in validation)\n- Update `lib/turn/apply.ts` to handle relationship updates\n- Add relationship display in LeftColumn NPC section\n\nDemo: Talk to Lenna → get personality-appropriate response → relationship can increase → visible in UI.\n\n---\n\n**Task 4: Implement Lenna (Scholar) with Token Reward**\n\nObjective: Lenna provides directions, lore, and relationship-gated token gift.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Add Lenna's full data to seed: shy/enthusiastic personality, dialogue hints about waystone research, career struggles\n- Create \"Lenna's Token\" item definition (trinket, mysterious quality)\n- Add logic to grant token when relationship reaches +2:\n  - In prompt, instruct LLM to offer token when relationship >= 2\n  - Validate `inventory_add` event for token\n- Lenna should naturally direct player toward Nomante Outpost\n\nDemo: Talk to Lenna multiple times, be nice → relationship hits +2 → receive token → token appears in inventory.\n\n---\n\n**Task 5: Implement Nomante Outpost NPCs**\n\nObjective: Add Aran, Adrian, and Helga with their personalities and offerings.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Add all three NPCs to seed data with distinct personalities:\n  - Aran: grizzled captain, practical, gives starter equipment\n  - Adrian: eager young ranger, Aran's right hand, gives hunting quest\n  - Helga: strong seasoned trader, gives berry quest\n- Update world state when player travels to outpost (entities change)\n- Implement equipment gifting from Aran (sword, leather armor, rations) as quest reward for \"Welcome to Windhollow\"\n\nDemo: Travel to outpost → see 3 NPCs → talk to each → distinct personalities → Aran gives starter gear.\n\n---\n\n**Task 6: Implement Quest System Integration**\n\nObjective: Enable quest acceptance, progress tracking, and completion flow.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Create quest acceptance flow: NPC offers quest → player accepts → quest added to character's active quests\n- Implement quest progress updates via `quest_progress` event type\n- Add quest completion detection and rewards\n- Display active quests in LeftColumn with progress indicators\n- Wire up quest leads as suggested actions\n\nDemo: Talk to Adrian → offered Boar Hunt quest → accept → quest appears in UI with leads.\n\n---\n\n**Task 7: Implement \"Welcome to Windhollow\" Quest**\n\nObjective: Tutorial quest from Lenna to visit outpost and meet Aran.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Quest auto-starts after talking to Lenna (or explicitly accepted)\n- Progress: 1) Leave waystone, 2) Arrive at outpost, 3) Talk to Aran\n- Completion triggers Aran giving starter equipment\n- Equipment: Simple Sword (mainHand), Used Leather Armor (chest), Rations x3 (consumable)\n\nDemo: Follow Lenna's directions → arrive at outpost → talk to Aran → quest completes → receive gear → equipped items visible.\n\n---\n\n**Task 8: Implement \"The Boar Hunt\" Quest**\n\nObjective: Combat tutorial quest from Adrian.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Adrian offers quest after player has starter equipment\n- Quest stages: 1) Accept quest, 2) Track boar (optional Survival check for bonus), 3) Kill boar\n- Add wild boar enemy template: trivial/easy tier, ~8 HP, 1d4 damage\n- Combat flow: player attacks → skill check → damage applied → boar HP tracked → death triggers completion\n- Rewards: 15 gold, Raw Meat item, +1 Adrian relationship, Hunting Bow (ranged weapon)\n\nDemo: Accept quest → go to wilderness → optional tracking → find boar → combat → kill it → rewards granted.\n\n---\n\n**Task 9: Implement \"Berry Gathering\" Quest**\n\nObjective: Exploration quest from Helga teaching skill checks.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Helga offers quest, describes \"rare mysterious berries\" (actually just blueberries she likes)\n- Quest stages: 1) Accept, 2) Search prairie, 3) Identify berries (Perception check DC 10), 4) Return to Helga\n- Success: find blueberries, return for reward\n- Failure: can retry the check, or return empty-handed\n- Rewards: 10 gold, +1 Helga relationship, Blueberry Pie (consumable, heals)\n\nDemo: Accept quest → explore wilderness → roll Perception → succeed → return → get pie.\n\n---\n\n**Task 10: Implement The Wanderer Random Encounter**\n\nObjective: Mysterious NPC with 10-20% encounter chance when traveling.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Add encounter chance logic when player moves between locations\n- Roll 1-100, if ≤15 (15% chance), add Wanderer to scene\n- Wanderer dialogue: cryptic, hints at larger mysteries, never direct answers\n- If player pushes for info (detected via intent), Wanderer leaves\n- No quest, no rewards, pure atmosphere\n\nDemo: Travel between locations multiple times → occasionally encounter Wanderer → cryptic dialogue → pushes away if pressed.\n\n---\n\n**Task 11: Implement Location Travel System**\n\nObjective: Enable movement between Waystone, Outpost, and Wilderness.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Detect travel intent: \"go to outpost\", \"head to waystone\", \"explore prairie\"\n- Update world state: poi, description, entities\n- Wilderness is the \"between\" state with random encounter chance\n- Add travel narration describing the journey\n- Update nearby_poi based on current location\n\nDemo: \"Go to the outpost\" → narration of walking through prairie → arrive at outpost → UI updates.\n\n---\n\n**Task 12: Demo Flow Testing & Polish**\n\nObjective: Verify 20-turn scenario works end-to-end, fix bugs, polish UX.\n\nImplementation guidance:\n- Test complete flow: create character → Lenna → outpost → all 3 quests → combat → completion\n- Verify all state changes persist correctly\n- Add loading states for quest/NPC data\n- Improve error messages for edge cases\n- Ensure streaming works smoothly throughout\n- Test Wanderer encounter triggers correctly\n\nDemo: Play through 20+ turns hitting all content without errors.\n\n---\n\nDoes this plan look good, or would you like me to adjust anything?"
